From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Turcios <turcioskevinr@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:30:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Silence ORT warnings again when building the face analyser

_build_face_analysis bypasses FaceAnalysis.__init__, which also called
onnxruntime.set_default_logger_severity(3). Without it, det_10g run below
its 640px export size logs nine output-shape warnings on every call. On
CUDA that more than doubled the detector run (8.7 ms vs 4.0 ms on an RTX
4060): detection 10.2 -> 5.7 ms per frame, live pipeline (HyperSwap 1c)
30.7 -> 36.3 fps, with GPEN-256 21.3 -> 23.9 fps. No change on Apple
Silicon, where the detector already uses a static-shape copy.

Applio-Commit: 91c8719df8b15fb1f06c819a197a7160044d64b1
---
 _vendor/modules/face_analyser.py | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/_vendor/modules/face_analyser.py b/_vendor/modules/face_analyser.py
index ddb89cc..195a6ab 100644
--- a/_vendor/modules/face_analyser.py
+++ b/_vendor/modules/face_analyser.py
@@ -52,6 +52,13 @@ def _build_face_analysis(providers) -> Any:
     unused models and the cached ``det_10g_coreml*`` copies, which on CoreML
     means several wasted compiles at startup.
     """
+    import onnxruntime
+
+    # FaceAnalysis.__init__ (bypassed here) silences ORT warnings. Keep that:
+    # det_10g run below its 640px export size logs nine output-shape
+    # warnings per call otherwise, which more than doubled detection time
+    # on CUDA (8.7 ms vs 4.0 ms on an RTX 4060).
+    onnxruntime.set_default_logger_severity(3)
     model_dir = os.path.join(os.path.expanduser("~"), ".insightface", "models", "buffalo_l")
     analyser = insightface.app.FaceAnalysis.__new__(insightface.app.FaceAnalysis)
     analyser.model_dir = model_dir
